WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.368
Host: Explain how venous pressure and
lymphatic obstruction can both produce fluid
accumulation.

2
00:00:06.368 --> 00:00:12.067
Guide: Higher venous pressure can increase
capillary hydrostatic pressure and filtration.

3
00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:17.775
Guide: Lymphatic obstruction reduces the route
that returns filtered fluid and proteins.

4
00:00:17.775 --> 00:00:23.369
Guide: Both can increase interstitial fluid,
but through different parts of the balance.

5
00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:31.182
Host: Two examples cause oedema: increased
venous pressure and lymphatic obstruction.
What differs?

6
00:00:31.182 --> 00:00:35.876
Guide: One can increase filtration; the other
reduces return.

7
00:00:35.876 --> 00:00:40.214
Guide: They change different sides of the
filtration–return balance.
